# Copy to `apps/server/.env` (gitignored) for NON-INTERACTIVE Wrangler auth
# (scripts). For local use, `wrangler login` is preferred and needs nothing here.
#
# IMPORTANT: Wrangler 4 also exposes `.env` keys to Worker code during local
# development unless `apps/server/.dev.vars` exists. If you use this file, copy
# `.dev.vars.example` to `.dev.vars` before running `wrangler dev`; Wrangler will
# then use `.dev.vars` (not `.env`) for the local Worker's runtime environment.
#
# Create a token at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
# with the "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template, scoped to the deployment account.
# This repo needs Workers Scripts + D1 + Workers Observability — Write and Account
# Settings — Read. Workers Routes — Write and Workers Tail — Read are optional.
# Durable Objects are covered by Workers Scripts — Write.
#
# In CI these are GitHub Actions repo secrets, not a file.

CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""

# --- NOT here ---
# Worker RUNTIME secrets (AUTH_SECRET, RT_TICKET_SECRET, …) go in
# `apps/server/.dev.vars` for local dev (see .dev.vars.example) and are set in
# production with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
